msgid "The marked point shows the basic overhead message. In this fit, reaching the illustrative per-round target at $p = 10^{-3}$ requires distance $d \\approx 21$, or about $881$ physical qubits per logical qubit using the bare rotated-patch count $2d^2-1$. This is not a full architecture-level resource estimate. A real fault-tolerant system must also budget syndrome-extraction circuits, decoding latency, routing, logical operations, and non-Clifford resources (the universal-gate machinery of Part 4). We focus now on the scaling pressure that motivates looking beyond strictly 2D-local codes.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng may markang punto ang pangunahing mensahe tungkol sa overhead. Sa fit na ito, ang pag-abot sa illustrative na per-round target sa $p = 10^{-3}$ ay nangangailangan ng distansyang $d \\approx 21$, o humigit-kumulang $881$ physical qubit bawat logical qubit gamit ang bare rotated-patch na bilang na $2d^2-1$. Hindi ito kumpletong resource estimate sa antas ng architecture. Ang isang tunay na fault-tolerant na sistema ay kailangan ding maglaan ng budget para sa mga syndrome-extraction circuit, decoding latency, routing, logical operation, at non-Clifford na resources (ang universal-gate machinery ng Part 4). Nakatuon tayo ngayon sa scaling pressure na nag-uudyok na tumingin sa labas ng mahigpit na 2D-local na mga code.\n"

